#
# Committed gzipped and served with Content-Encoding: gzip. The bundle is 1.4 MB
# raw and 409 KB compressed, and doing it here costs no build-time compressor and
# no runtime decompressor -- every browser accepts gzip.
#
# `gzip -9 -n`: -n leaves the modification time out of the header, so
# recompressing the same input gives the same bytes and the hashes below are
# something a reader can reproduce.
#
# Each section is named for the file committed here. Two hashes: `upstream` is of
# the file as downloaded, *before* compression, so the download can be checked
# against what was actually vendored. `committed` is of the
# gzipped file in this directory, and it is the one
# tests/core/test_remote_assets.cpp asserts the embedded bytes match -- a
# committed minified blob is opaque to review, and that test is what makes an
# accidental or malicious replacement loud rather than invisible.
#
# To update: download the two files at the new version, check them against the
# upstream hashes the release publishes, `gzip -9 -n` them, and put the new
# numbers here. The test fails until they agree.

